const precisPYQ=[
 ["PYQ",2025,"Reported précis task on road construction","Write a précis of the supplied practice passage while preserving its central idea and key points.","Identify the central argument, remove examples and repetition, retain the essential facts, and give a concise suitable title.","PRACTICE RECONSTRUCTION — This is an original passage based on the reported topic, not the original 2025 question paper passage. Road construction can improve mobility, connect markets and support access to schools, hospitals and employment. Yet the value of a road project depends on more than its length. Poor planning can create drainage problems, traffic bottlenecks, environmental damage and unnecessary maintenance costs. Authorities therefore need to assess local needs before construction and consider the effect on nearby communities. Good roads should be supported by safe junctions, pedestrian facilities, drainage and regular maintenance. Transparent procurement and monitoring can also reduce delays and cost overruns. When projects are planned with long-term use in mind, public investment can produce wider economic and social benefits. The objective should not simply be to build more roads, but to create reliable and safe connections that serve people efficiently over time."],
 ["PYQ",2024,"Reported précis task on Artificial Intelligence — opportunities and challenges","Write a précis of the supplied practice passage while preserving its central idea and key points.","Retain the main opportunities and risks, remove illustrations and repetition, and write in your own words.","PRACTICE RECONSTRUCTION — This is an original passage based on the reported topic, not the original 2024 question paper passage. Artificial intelligence can increase productivity by helping people analyse information, automate repetitive work and support faster decisions. Its benefits, however, depend on how responsibly it is designed and used. Poor-quality data can produce biased results, while excessive automation may weaken human oversight. The collection and processing of personal information also create privacy concerns. Organisations therefore need clear accountability, appropriate testing and ways for people to challenge or correct important decisions. Workers may also need opportunities to develop new skills as tasks change. AI should not be viewed simply as a replacement for human effort. Its most useful role may be to support people while leaving important judgement, responsibility and ethical decisions under human control."],
]
SF.sbi.precis.push(...precisPYQ);
